{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d627","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0741b-6622-7cb3-8912-9b715d19fde5"},"sequence":2414,"recorded_at":1780531400004823,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"299e9e89-8e07-4f61-8116-490e98862efb","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"299e9e89-8e07-4f61-8116-490e98862efb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"299e9e89-8e07-4f61-8116-490e98862efb"},"call_id":"call_01a0742c2b6674e2b7f2a9ba8f4687f8","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-55-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 30 LOGBOOK.md 2>&1\\ndate '+%Y-%m-%d %H%M'\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook format and date\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-05\\n\\n### 0935 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-6 rework: switch vocabularies, ExecRunner frame loss, flake bound\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-6 verdict (changes requested, two blocking findings F1/F2 plus the nondeterministic suite). Carries the reviewer's findings into the logbook — the reviewer deliberately left LOGBOOK.md out of their delta. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (F1, blocking): the three switch-shaped closed vocabularies the census could not see (envelope member set `checkResponseMembers` ← `DecodeResponse:416`, execution profile `ProfileMapping` ← `DecodeSpawnPlan:100`, transaction state `validStatusState` ← `DecodeStatusOutcome:126`) are package-level maps now (`responseMembers`, `profileNames`, `statusStates`), each consulted by a membership check, so the existing census derives them with no scanner change. Each carries a pinned-document derivation (`TestResponseMembersAreDerivedFromSpec` from the two 7.2 envelope sentences with `ok = true/false` normalized, `TestProfileNamesAreDerivedFromSpec` from the two 7.7 profile sentences with exactly-one-span guards, `TestStatusStatesAreDerivedFromSpec` from the 7.5 ProviderTransactionStatus state span), a census registration (19 → 22 vocabularies, both directions), and a production entry-point refusal row (envelope/`bogus` via DecodeResponse, `ProfileMapping(codex, bogus)`, bogus status state via DecodeStatusOutcome). `TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified` pins the residue: every production switch must be a classified dispatch (the one remaining switch dispatches on an already-validated state), so a new switch-shaped gate fails until classified. The \\\"closes the class by construction\\\" header now states the derived shapes plus this guard instead of an unstated-empty residue.\\n- FIX (F2, blocking): `ExecRunner` discarded judgeable results through two races on `Host.Call`'s primary path. (a) `return Result{}, writeErr` before stdout was ever considered: an EPIPE racing the plugin's exit threw away valid correlated frames. (b) Found during this rework by driving `Run` directly (2 of 20 crash-script iters returned `read |0: file already closed`): `Wait` closes `StdoutPipe`/`StderrPipe` read ends after seeing the process exit, racing a drain still in flight — this, not EPIPE, is what misclassified the stdin-draining `exit 3` fixture. Fix per the file's own comments: judge whenever possible (non-empty stdout governs; empty stdout with a known exit classifies the crash through the Result), surface write/close/wait failures only with empty stdout and no known exit, and drain over `os.Pipe` pairs owned by `Run` so no later Close can interrupt a drain. New tests `TestExecRunnerKeepsValidFrameWhenPluginIgnoresStdin` (200 calls, zero discards) and `TestExecRunnerClassifiesCrashExitDeterministically` (50 crash calls, all `plugin exited without a response`): both FAIL on the pre-fix runner (2/200 frames discarded; crash misclassified as `runner reported no result`, each verified by swapping the pre-fix `runner.go` back with sha256-verified restore) and pass post-fix.\\n- FLAKE BOUND: post-fix `go test ./internal/provhost/ -count=1` 30/30 green in two 15-run chunks (pre-fix: 3 red in 50 per the reviewer). The two F2 loops above are the deterministic pins; the old single-shot `TestExecRunnerReportsCrashExit` stays as a third witness.\\n- EVIDENCE: `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `GOOS=windows go vet ./internal/provhost/` exit 0; gofmt clean; `go test ./... -count=1` green (15 packages); provhost `-race` green; provhost cover 86.5% → 86.0% (new judge/pipe branches). Widening mutants re-planted against the new maps (envelope/profile/status `\\\"bogus\\\"`, plus an unclassified-switch plant): each dies three ways — derivation, census subtest, entry-point row — with cp-aside/sha256 restores; the one vacuous-green run in the sequence (a gofmt-realigned anchor that planted nothing) was caught by the grep-plant assertion and re-run with the corrected anchor.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0926 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-6 rework: the vocabulary class closed by census\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-5 verdict (changes requested, single blocking finding F1r). Test-only rework: new `internal/provhost/closed_vocabulary_census_test.go`, `requireVocabulary` comparison fix in `closed_vocabularies_test.go`. Production untouched; uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (F1r): the nine membership-checked vocabularies with no derivation (manifest/probe/capability/identity/identify/quiesce/spawn/status member sets plus the yolo mapping) are now derived from the pinned document — example-JSON keys for 7.3/7.4, first-sentence code spans for the capability-value sentence, TableRowAt Field rows for the 5.5 identity table, per-span member declarations for the 7.5 SpawnPlan/SafeBoundaryProof/ProviderTransactionStatus rows, braced-cell parsing for the identify-session success body, per-row provider-plus-first-flag for the 7.7 table. The census parses production source for package-level []string/map[string]bool/map[string]string with membership use (unknownMember argument, map index, range operand) and requires each of the 19 found vocabularies to carry an executing derivation, in both directions.\\n- EVIDENCE: probe_widen.json replay, full-package runs, cp+sha256 restores: W1–W9 KILLED (each red three ways — derivation, census subtest, entry-point refusal row), W10/R2/R4 killed, R1/R3 survive as the stated behaviour-preserving bounds. Fail-closed attacks all red: wrong type name, bad cell marker, off-table identity window, unregistered planted vocabulary (`has no registered spec derivation`), blinded string-map scan (`names no production vocabulary`), dropped registration. `requireVocabulary` now uses reflect.DeepEqual, so the V4 joined-member mutant is killed by the derivation alone. Gates: build/vet/GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` 15/15 green, provhost -race green, provhost cover 86.5% unchanged. CORRECTION (round-6 review): the \\\"15/15 green\\\" was one observation of a nondeterministic suite, not a property — the clean tree failed `go test ./internal/provhost/` 3 times in 50 runs under load (F2 below). Green-suite claims now carry a run count.\\n- ANOMALY: the capability-value sentence shares its window with the warnings sentence, so a naive span read derives five members including warnings; the derivation truncates to the declaring sentence. The bare 5.5 closed sentence repeats in four sections, so the identity quote carries its schema opener to stay unique. The *Required order lists are excluded from the census by construction (missingMember-only use), which is what keeps R1/R3 surviving.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\\n\\n### 0830 — Provider conformance-harness leaf round-5 rework: the 28 real survivors, closed by derivation\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti round-4 verdict (changes requested, 106 mutants, 76 killed, 30 survived, 2 stated bounds, 28 real). Test-only rework in `internal/provhost` plus one comment restatement; production untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\\n- FIX (F1, blocking): the eight closed vocabularies the three existing specdoc derivations did not cover are now derived the same way in `internal/provhost/closed_vocabularies_test.go` — probe statuses and evidence from the Section 7.4 sentences, architectures from 7.4 prose cross-checked against the 7.5 probe request row, probe platforms from that row (sorted both sides: the row lists macos first, the implementation holds sorted order), quiesce blockers from the 7.5 enum sentence, identity kinds from the 5.5 table row, identify confidence and matched-evidence from the 7.5 identify-session row. Each widening mutant from the verdict battery (partial, assumed, 386, freebsd, other, legacy_alias, guess, guessed) is killed twice: once by the derivation equality, once by an exact-member refusal row through the production entry point.\\n- FIX (F2): last-element substitution rows for both manifest order loops, first-element-unknown platform row (aix, still sorted-unique so it reaches the vocab check), and first/last missing-registry-key probe rows.\\n- FIX (F3): NUL-injection fixtures for both SpawnPlan members that reach exec — argv element and env-literal value — via JSON `\\\\u0000` escapes.\\n2026-09-06 0444\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8531,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2133,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
