{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d6b3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0741b-6622-7cb3-8912-9b715d19fde5"},"sequence":2484,"recorded_at":1780531400004963,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"299e9e89-8e07-4f61-8116-490e98862efb","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"299e9e89-8e07-4f61-8116-490e98862efb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"299e9e89-8e07-4f61-8116-490e98862efb"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"70f0bba8-7efa-46de-acda-9c59c7a4d296"},"task_id":"70f0bba8-7efa-46de-acda-9c59c7a4d296","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"70f0bba8-7efa-46de-acda-9c59c7a4d296","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-05\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-06\n+\n+### 0444 — Session-adapter leaf rework: all four blocking verdict findings closed, one anomaly reported\n+\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-2z3se0 round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, F1–F4 blocking + F5–F7). All changes inside `internal/sessadapter/`; previously reviewed files untouched. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n+- FIX (F1): nine inline closed unions → table loops with `valid*` consultants (mode, direction, entry status, registry-entry status, evidence result, candidate kind, role, context-free ops). Refusal details byte-identical, 323-arm inventory unchanged. Census scanner extended two ways: named slice/map types resolve package-wide; new `TestNoUnregisteredInlineVocabularies` forbids any chain comparing one operand against 2+ closed values. The new detector immediately found two more real unions (probe candidate kind, manifest/probe context dispatch) the reviewer had not listed. Spec pins for all eight unions; registrations 55 → 63.\n+- FIX (F2): `collectFileArms` exempts only the definition Name in its ValueSpec; `var x = ctor` fails package-level and function-local. `TestConstructorAliasSpellingsFailDerivation` replays all four probes on synthetic sources.\n+- FIX (F3): `TestSurrogatePairSweep` — every high × {lowLo−1, lowLo, lowHi, lowHi+1} plus full-range interior for three highs, verdicts from test-local literals: 2058 refused + 5124 admitted.\n+- FIX (F4): per-member drivers for doctor-required (4×2 writer variants), nullability (4×2 branches, request side), applicable checks (3) + nullable-bool types (3).\n+- FIX (F5/F6/F7): same-length echo forgery; exact/over frame edges on all three envelopes; four zero-value host-fact refusals.\n+- EVIDENCE: narrowing-mutant battery 26 killed + 1 control-green / 27 measured, every mutant grep-confirmed present and compiling before its verdict (`/tmp/mutant-battery.py`, log attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-battery-rev2.log`). Gates: `go test ./...` 17/17 exit 0, sessadapter 904 PASS/0 FAIL, `-count=3` green, `-race` green, cover 81.1% → 81.4%, vet + GOOS=windows vet exit 0, gofmt clean.\n+- ANOMALY (behavior preserved, needs product decision): `checkValidateNullability` is shared by request and success bodies, but validate success bodies carry no target members and the member set is exact, so archive-mode success ALWAYS refuses (`carries a target member` on absent members, reproduced with a scratch test) while staged/live success passes vacuously — the success-side call is a mode gate in disguise. F4 driven request-side where the rule is well-defined. Options: scope the rule to requests / redesign absent-handling / declare archive success impossible.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n+\n+## 2026-09-05\n"}}}
